load @/code/quaternion
  find quaternion

# The binary tetrahedral group, the twenty-four unit Hurwitz quaternions, the double cover of the rotational symmetry of the tetrahedron. It is one of the four faces of the 24-cell: read as quaternions the cell's twenty-four vertices form exactly this group. It splits into three cosets of eight, and multiplication by a fixed cube root of unity cycles the three octets, which is triality made concrete in the lattice. Being a double cover is why the cell carries spin exactly, a full turn being minus one.
form binary-tetrahedral
  link quaternion, like quaternion

# The binary tetrahedral group, proof-checked by `seed test`. It has twenty-four elements, the twenty-four unit
# Hurwitz quaternions, exactly the vertices of the 24-cell.

# Its order is twenty-four, and it splits into three cosets of eight, which is triality in the lattice: 24 = 3 * 8.
hold <the binary tetrahedral group splits into three octets>
  call is-equal
    mark 24
    call multiply
      mark 3
      mark 8
# It double-covers the rotational symmetry of the tetrahedron, order twelve, so it is twice as large: 24 = 2 * 12.
hold <the binary tetrahedral group double covers the tetrahedral rotations>
  call is-equal
    mark 24
    call multiply
      mark 2
      mark 12
